  "worked_solution": "Since we are given both the value of $\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(\\pi )\u2016$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{\u03ba(t)}=\\frac{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(\\pi )=\u27e8-1,-\\pi \u27e9$,  since the point $P(-1,-\\pi )$ is at the tip of $r(\\pi ).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{\u2032}(t)$, ${T}^{\u2032}(\\pi )$ and $\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(\\pi )\u2016$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)\u27e9=\u27e8-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\u27e9 \\\\ {T}^{\u2032}(\\pi ) & =\u27e8-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\pi ,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\pi \u27e9=\u27e80,1\u27e9 \\\\ \u2016{T}^{\u2032}(\\pi )\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\pi ) & =\\frac{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(\\pi )\u2016}{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(\\pi )\u2016}=\\frac{\\pi }{1}=\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=\\pi $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(\\pi ) & =\\frac{{T}^{\u2032}(\\pi )}{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(\\pi )\u2016}=\u27e80,1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\pi )+R(\\pi )N(\\pi ) & =\u27e8-1,-\\pi \u27e9+\\pi \u27e80,1\u27e9=\u27e8-1,0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
